    {
      "id": "c2064a81-7ec4-4534-9694-f61012c6293f",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 0,
      "data": {
        "title": "OSM por dentro"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "07e66b94-88eb-464d-9ddd-55aba474a91a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "OpenStreetMap é o \"Wikipedia dos mapas\" — base global colaborativa, em PT-BR comunidade ativa. Para apps de mapas próprios em 2026, OSM + MapLibre é o stack open-source padrão, oferecendo independência de Google/Mapbox."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "516b3cc1-5c64-42b5-bbec-6a470ebb8d58",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 1,
      "data": {
        "title": "Formatos e fontes"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "de7970fe-f5d4-47b5-9c08-fbeab7f3531c",
          "type": "key_value",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "items": [
              {
                "k": "XML (.osm)",
                "v": "Formato canônico, verboso. ~150GB descompactado para planet."
              },
              {
                "k": "PBF (.osm.pbf)",
                "v": "Protocol Buffer binário, ~70-90GB planet. Padrão para download/processing."
              },
              {
                "k": "Diffs",
                "v": "minutely.osc / hourly.osc / daily.osc — incrementais para sync contínuo"
              },
              {
                "k": "Extracts regionais",
                "v": "Geofabrik (download.geofabrik.de) tem PBF por país/estado (Brasil ~3GB)"
              },
              {
                "k": "Overpass API",
                "v": "Queries ad-hoc sem download (overpass-api.de)"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "45d9edac-529d-4b1a-8e1e-cebe8580044c",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 2,
      "data": {
        "title": "Overpass query — exemplo"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "72ec09fd-97df-4124-a150-ce483cb49639",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "language": "text",
            "code": "# Todos cafés em São Paulo (Overpass QL)\n[out:json][timeout:25];\narea[\"name\"=\"São Paulo\"]->.searchArea;\n(\n  node[\"amenity\"=\"cafe\"](area.searchArea);\n  way[\"amenity\"=\"cafe\"](area.searchArea);\n);\nout body;\n>;\nout skel qt;"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dfe52738-8733-47a1-b3e3-961a79fc0f4b",
          "type": "callout",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "variant": "info",
            "title": "",
            "content": "Teste no overpass-turbo.eu — UI gráfica para Overpass QL com visualização."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c66078a4-876e-46c3-b1af-b22255394f83",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 3,
      "data": {
        "title": "Pipeline de produção"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "1c7aaf38-1ffa-41ce-9773-560580a2076a",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "language": "bash",
            "code": "# 1. Baixar PBF Brasil\ncurl -O https://download.geofabrik.de/south-america/brazil-latest.osm.pbf\n\n# 2. Filtrar (osmium) — só estradas e POIs\nosmium tags-filter brazil-latest.osm.pbf \\\n  highway amenity building \\\n  -o brazil-filtered.osm.pbf\n\n# 3. Carregar Postgres+PostGIS\nosm2pgsql --create --slim --hstore \\\n  --cache 8000 \\\n  --number-processes 8 \\\n  --database osm brazil-filtered.osm.pbf\n\n# 4. Gerar vector tiles (tippecanoe)\ntippecanoe -o brazil.mbtiles \\\n  --maximum-zoom=14 --minimum-zoom=4 \\\n  --drop-densest-as-needed \\\n  brazil-filtered.geojson\n\n# 5. Servir via Martin\nmartin --pg postgres://localhost/osm\n\n# 6. Sync diário (osmupdate + diffs)\nosmupdate brazil-latest.osm.pbf brazil-new.osm.pbf"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fe6b70cb-68f2-4c95-9905-7e2b0b69d54a",
